<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cyclic and dihedral subgroups of <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Mod_{0}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Mod</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Mod_{0}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> The following tables for <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\leq n\leq 13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\leq n\leq 13</annotation></semantics></math> come directly form <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3. ‣ 3.1. Finite subgroups of Mod_0^𝑛 and their realization ‣ 3. Genus 0 ‣ The proper geometric dimension of the mapping class group of an orientable surface with punctures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. Note that in all these cases <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vcd(WF)+\lambda(F)\leq\vcd(\Mod_{0}^{n})=n-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>vcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>vcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Mod</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vcd(WF)+\lambda(F)\leq\vcd(\Mod_{0}^{n})=n-3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T2" class="ltx_table">
