<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span><math id="A2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(F)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vcd(WF)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>vcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vcd(WF)</annotation></semantics></math> for finite subgroups of <math id="A2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Mod_{2}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Mod</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Mod_{2}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix we use Broughton’s classification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bro91</a>, Theorem 4.1 <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> Table 4]</cite> to give upper bounds for <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vcd(WF)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>vcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vcd(WF)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(F)</annotation></semantics></math> for all the conjugacy classes of non-trivial finite subgroups <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Mod_{2}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Mod</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Mod_{2}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
